  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Ren Xiu Ping’s grandson carries Ren Xiu Ping’s traveling son Gu in the turbulent flow sea area and says he can return to doting mother Gu, which is with his grandfather. He activates it as traveling son Immortal Gu when that space is about to collapse, and its power sends him into Ren Xiu Ping’s blessed land.",
        "chapters": [
          1156
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_ren_xiu_ping",
          "gu_doting_mother_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Both belong to emotion path. Emotion path originates from wisdom path, with thoughts, wills, and emotions as its three elements. In the turbulent flow sea area, chaotic dao marks keep Gu Immortals from using space path Immortal Gu easily; he can use traveling son Gu without any danger because emotion path had not been created when that sea area formed.",
        "chapters": [
          1156
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "pair-and-path",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "path_emotion",
          "path_wisdom",
          "sys_gu_immortal",
          "sys_immortal_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Shen Shang names traveling son Gu and doting mother Gu as examples of human emotion and virtue Gu among human path Gu worms. The same stretch states they were once regarded as emotion path Gu worms, but in essence were actually human path.",
